<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Proposal 21 L3b. THE PLACEMENT CONVERSION (design D6), gated end to end.

  Env, set on the CTest entry (see smaragd/CMakeLists.txt) because the runner
  reads it at the first createAudioInput() call, long after the script is
  parsed:
    SMARAGD_AUDIO_INPUT_BACKEND=file:../test_position.wav
    SMARAGD_AUDIO_INPUT_LATENCY_FRAMES=4800     the driver's CLAIM
    SMARAGD_CAPTURE_SPEED=1                     RUN_SERIAL, real time
  The input is the position-encoded fixture (tw303a/analysis/tools/
  gen_position_fixture -verify): a 4096-frame block staircase whose block k
  decodes to frame k, so a decoded value IS a capture-frame index.

  WHAT IS A CLOSED FORM HERE, AND WHAT DELIBERATELY IS NOT.

  P0 - the project frame that capture frame 0's host time maps to - depends
  on when the capture thread and the render callback actually ran, so it is
  NOT predictable and nothing below asserts it. What IS exact, in integers, is
  the COMPENSATION the conversion applied:

      compensation = -inputLatency - outputLatency + userOffset

  inputLatency is 4800 (this case sets it); outputLatency is the capture
  backend's own buffer, 1024 frames (capture_backend.cc: outputLatencyFrames =
  bufferFrames), at the project rate on a device whose rate the capture backend
  adopts, so the projectRate/deviceRate scaling is exactly 1. Hence

      offset 0    ->  compensation = -4800 - 1024        = -5824
      offset +20  ->  compensation = -5824 - 960         = -6784

  and the difference is EXACTLY 960 frames = 20 ms at 48 kHz, EARLIER, which is
  the sign convention SSettings::recordingOffsetMs documents (positive = the
  driver under-reports, compensate more, place the audio earlier).

  assert-recorded-clip also checks the IDENTITY internally on every call -
  the clip's actual link start must equal placementFrame(trimmed) - so a
  recorder that reported the right terms and applied different ones fails here
  even though every expectation above would pass.

  THE PHYSICAL CLAIM is sourceAtStartFrame: the position-encoded value decoded
  at the placed clip's first content frame must equal the number of capture
  frames the mapping says were trimmed (0 here, because the transport was
  already running). That is faithfulness - every frame the file produced
  reached the pages in order, none lost or duplicated between the device ring,
  the bridge thread, the growing capture source and the placement - and it is
  what "the placed clip's positions read true" means. The tolerance is one
  DECODE block (4096): the decoder resolves 4096-frame blocks by construction.

  The transport is deliberately PLAYING before the take, so an anchor exists at
  once and nothing is trimmed. Recording from a STOPPED transport is the
  retrospective-mapping path and is covered by record_punch.
-->
<SActionScript version="1" name="record_offset_zero">

  <setup project="new"/>

  <actions>
    <add-track index="-1"/>
    <add-track index="-1"/>

    <!-- Monitoring off: this case is about the PLACEMENT, and a live lane
         would put the input into the capture backend as well, which is
         monitor_through_chain's job. -->
    <set-monitor-mode trackPath="0" mode="off"/>
    <set-monitor-mode trackPath="1" mode="off"/>

    <!-- TAKE 1: offset 0. .................................................. -->
    <set-option key="audio/recordingOffsetMs/default" value="0"/>
    <arm-track trackPath="0" armed="1"/>
    <set-locator position="0"/>
    <toggle-playback play="1"/>
    <wait-playhead minAdvance="4096" timeoutMs="30000"/>
    <wait-ms ms="500"/>
    <record-start/>
    <wait-ms ms="1500"/>
    <record-stop/>

    <assert-recorded-clip trackPath="0" clips="1" passes="1"
                          inputLatencyFrames="4800"
                          outputLatencyFrames="1024"
                          userOffsetFrames="0"
                          compensationFrames="-5824"
                          trimmedFrames="0"
                          sourceAtStartFrame="0" sourceTolerance="4096"
                          minDurationFrames="24000"/>

    <!-- TAKE 2: offset +20 ms == 960 frames EARLIER. ....................... -->
    <set-option key="audio/recordingOffsetMs/default" value="20"/>
    <arm-track trackPath="1" armed="1"/>
    <set-locator position="0"/>
    <toggle-playback play="1"/>
    <wait-playhead minAdvance="4096" timeoutMs="30000"/>
    <wait-ms ms="500"/>
    <record-start/>
    <wait-ms ms="1500"/>
    <record-stop/>

    <assert-recorded-clip trackPath="1" clips="1" passes="1"
                          inputLatencyFrames="4800"
                          outputLatencyFrames="1024"
                          userOffsetFrames="-960"
                          compensationFrames="-6784"
                          trimmedFrames="0"
                          sourceAtStartFrame="0" sourceTolerance="4096"
                          minDurationFrames="24000"/>

    <!-- This case OWNS audio/recordingOffsetMs/default; put it back. -->
    <set-option key="audio/recordingOffsetMs/default" value="0"/>

    <assert-render-policy liveThreadRefusals="0" liveOwnedRefusals="0"/>
  </actions>

  <assertions>
    <assert-track-count equals="2"/>
  </assertions>

</SActionScript>
